& [Purpose]
  + implement SWA-07 P0 as the smallest provider-free end-to-end correspondence join over the existing unmodified SWA-01 through SWA-04A and SWA-06A forms
  + prove that one exact update-intent checkpoint is a prefix of the later exact succeeding-SOP checkpoint with an attributable bridge
  + stop at supplied-data correspondence without physical work update publication semantic review signature or activation

& [RequestAndUpstream]
  + [PFC-001] profiles are cantor-provider-free-self-work-composition-request/0.1 and cantor-provider-free-self-work-composition-receipt/0.1 with strict closed deterministic JSON
  + [PFC-002] request embeds and revalidates one complete SWA-04A handoff request and one complete SWA-06A succeeding-SOP request through their owning public validators
  + [PFC-003] both embedded requests carry exactly equal complete SelfWorkLifecycleRequest values and composition identity is distinct from all causal identities
  + [PFC-004] handoff checkpoint transitions are an exact proper prefix of the succeeding checkpoint transitions and both checkpoints independently replay under the common lifecycle

& [CausalJoin]
  + [PFC-005] handoff selected step resolves exactly once to work-plan class propose_update and is the exact ready selected attempt at the prefix checkpoint
  + [PFC-006] the same selected update step and attempt are complete at the later checkpoint and at least one transition for that attempt occurs strictly after the prefix
  + [PFC-007] one bridge_evidence_ref is present in handoff evidence and in at least one post-prefix transition for the exact selected update step and attempt
  + [PFC-008] succeeding selected step resolves exactly once to class propose_succeeding_sop and remains the exact ready attempt required by unmodified SWA-06A validation

& [CompilationAndProjection]
  + [PFC-009] compiler deterministically recompiles the exact SWA-04A proposal and validates its prepared_awaiting_physical_revalidation representation-only output
  + [PFC-010] compiler deterministically recompiles the exact SWA-06A proposal and its self-contained machine correspondence verification receipt
  + [PFC-011] receipt projects exact composition boot plan lifecycle pre-update checkpoint handoff update-step later checkpoint succeeding-step succeeding proposal and verification identities through existing canonical digests
  + [PFC-012] status is provider_free_chain_correspondence_verified authority is supplied_data_correspondence_only physical_contact is false and a closed stage account names proposal_only prepared_not_executing update_not_performed and awaiting_independent_review
  + [PFC-013] exact nonauthority text denies authentication freshness process workspace provider model work test mutation verification acceptance rollback cleanup commit push semantic review signature persistence activation and external effects

& [DigestsVerificationAndFaults]
  + [PFC-014] request digest is domain-separated SHA-256 over the complete canonical request
  + [PFC-015] receipt digest is independently domain-separated SHA-256 over the complete receipt with only its own digest empty
  + [PFC-016] verifier recompiles the full expected receipt from the embedded request and requires complete equality without external state
  + [PFC-017] request and receipt machine forms are bounded to 16777216 bytes reject unknown fields and trailing content and replay byte-identically
  + [PFC-018] faults are typed for profile identity handoff succeeding lifecycle join step class bridge evidence authority correspondence digest bound and machine-form violations with atomic refusal
  + [PFC-019] implementation is one safe cantor_ecosystem module one export one stdin/stdout compile-or-verify CLI and has no process filesystem environment clock network provider model unsafe or output-path product surface
  + [PFC-020] focused semantic CLI static and evidence tests exact workspace debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied Clippy format recursive evidence local acceptance attribution publication and post-push replay pass with zero provider trials

& [Acceptance]
  + [PFC-A01] source manifest input audit data design twenty-threat review seven-fold exhaustion canonical explosion justification matrix plan phase lock proof readiness review and signature bind exactly
  + [PFC-A02] deterministic success covers the exact lifecycle prefix update completion bridge evidence succeeding proposal complete receipt both digests and strict machine forms
  + [PFC-A03] adversarial tests refuse downstream substitution lifecycle mismatch prefix splice wrong classes attempt/state mismatch bridge evidence omission or laundering authority projection digest unknown-field oversize extra-argument and output-path faults
  + [PFC-A04] static inspection proves no unsafe process filesystem environment clock network provider model publication signature activation or output-path surface and no dependency delta
  + [PFC-A05] independent evidence rehashes every governed artifact requires exact nonauthority and zero provider trials and joins recursive evidence acceptance attribution publication and replay

& [DualHemisphere]
  + semantic hemisphere preserves predecessor SOP objective plan exact update intent bridge evidence next-SOP source authorship and unresolved frontier
  + physical hemisphere preserves that every receipt is supplied data physical_contact is false and no work update publication review signature or activation occurred
  + convergence is one deterministic provider-free chain correspondence receipt with no imported authority

& [Delineation]
  + nested pure-form validation checkpoint-prefix comparison step-class and attempt continuity bridge-evidence membership recompilation projection digests machine verification and bounded CLI are inside
  + physical observation process workspace read or mutation test update verification acceptance rollback cleanup commit push provider model semantic review signature source persistence activation remote FPGA Minecraft and foreign work are outside

